From 79522997bb4e6c77ca3fc1c87c0dca592434ffdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Torben Haack <t128n@ipv4.8shield.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:13:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mail): let the sandboxed view document out of the opener
 policy and allow 'self' frame-src

`add_security_headers` set `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` on
every response. Per the HTML Living Standard, a nested browsing context
(like the reading pane iframe) must not load a `same-origin` response,
so Chromium, Firefox and Safari abort the navigation of
`/api/v1/mail/content/{token}` and the reading pane shows a broken
document instead of the message.

Additionally, the top-level Content Security Policy set `frame-src`
without `'self'` (`frame-src blob: ...`), which caused browsers to block
the reading pane iframe from navigating to `/api/v1/mail/content/{token}`.

A handler that sets its own CSP (the sandboxed mail view document, the
only one) now gets `unsafe-none` like its framing rules; its sandbox CSP
keeps the frame from reaching the app. Every other response still
isolates its opener. The top-level CSP includes `'self'` in `frame-src`.
Covered at the platform layer, and against the real document in the mail
content suite.

Fixes t128n/torbit#23, t128n/torbit#29.
